    "publishedAt": "2026-08-21 18:02:59",
    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.6 测试版\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n- 新增模型级“免费使用”开关。开启后保留模型原有计费配置与价格展示，新建任务按创建时快照免除费用。\n- 扩展风格库分类、推荐与排序能力，为现有 51 个内置风格补齐基础分类；管理员可继续维护分类、推荐状态和显示顺序。\n- 新增可灵 3.0 九类视频生成场景、MiniMax H3 视频生成 V2 与 Seedance 2.5 多模态视频生成，完善回调唤醒、轮询降级、生命周期控制和用量结算。\n- GPT Image 2 改为按生成张数计费；Seedance 2.0、2.0 Fast 与 2.5 按视频 Token 用量结算，并使用安全的预冻结与退款规则。\n- 文本模型新增思考协议、思考预算、输出上限及思考内容展示配置；计费支持聚合与互斥分桶两种口径，缓存和思考 Token 可独立计价。\n- 分镜脚本统一使用 `scenes[].shots[]` 场景归组，视频提示词使用稳定 `shotKey` 双向映射，并新增可选的直接上一镜连续性模式。\n- 图片、视频、语音和文本供应商统一支持可配置的提交路径与查询路径，兼容带前置目录的代理网关，并加强路径合法性校验。\n- Web 用户端完成 Next.js App Router、React、TypeScript、Ant Design React 与 Zustand 技术栈迁移，继续输出兼容现有部署器的 `dist/public` 静态产物。\n- 管理端统一模型、供应商、系统配置、错误治理、发布管理和系统管理页面的视觉与交互规范。\n- 在线源码升级新增构建资源治理：限制 Maven、Node.js、Go 和压缩阶段的 CPU、内存、Swap、进程数与 I/O；资源紧张时自动降速或暂停，恢复后继续。\n- 新安装默认关闭后台安全访问码，管理员可在系统配置中按需启用并设置访问路径。\n- 官方素材查询新增背景音乐类型；角色、场景和道具形态接口补齐可编辑的出图提示词，并兼容历史数据结构。\n- 本地 FFmpeg 整片合成支持保留视频原声，并正确混合配音与循环背景音乐；同时完善横竖屏分辨率、字幕字号、音画时长、旋转视频和超时进程清理，视频统一使用 `tpad` 补帧，音频统一使用定长 `apad`，多音轨使用 `amix normalize=0` 与 `alimiter`。\n- Docker、手动部署、初始化 SQL 与升级 SQL 统一使用 AID 自管 FFmpeg 7.0.2 固定运行时，默认路径为 `/opt/aid-ffmpeg/current/ffmpeg` 与 `/opt/aid-ffmpeg/current/ffprobe`，安装后无需修改后台。amd64、arm64 制品分别强制核对 SHA256，安装时统一验证 FFprobe、必要编码器、滤镜和 1 秒音视频合成；失败保留原运行时，完整版本幂等复用。\n- Docker 与手动部署新增统一中文字体初始化：优先复用经中文字符集与 `drawtext` 验证的系统字体；没有合格字体时安装固定的 Noto Sans SC 2.004 并校验 SHA256、保留 OFL 许可。默认路径为 `/opt/aid-fonts/current/aid-cjk-font`，升级不会覆盖已有自定义字体配置。\n- 修复文本任务预冻结与真实用量结算、分镜编辑器光标与引用插入、视频封面展示、项目画面比例、任务终态恢复、场景资产引用及多项创作流程稳定性问题。\n- 新增可重复执行的 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.6.sql`，升级已有数据库时保留管理员已配置的代理路径、倍率和有效自定义计费规则，并清理历史重复配置后补齐配置唯一索引。\n\n\u003e 本版本为 Beta 测试版。升级会在本机从版本标签构建三端程序。请先备份数据库和部署配置，并在测试环境验证模型计费、创作流程、文件存储和在线升级。低资源服务器会自动限速，构建时间可能相应延长。\n\n# AID v1.0.0-beta.6 Beta Release\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n- Added a per-model free-use switch. Existing pricing remains visible, while newly created tasks use a creation-time billing snapshot and can be charged at zero when enabled.\n- Expanded style categories, recommendations, and stable ordering. The existing 51 built-in styles now have baseline categories that administrators can maintain.\n- Added nine Kling 3.0 video scenarios, MiniMax H3 Video Generation V2, and Seedance 2.5 multimodal video generation with callback wake-up, polling fallback, lifecycle limits, and usage settlement.\n- Changed GPT Image 2 to per-image billing. Seedance 2.0, 2.0 Fast, and 2.5 now settle by video-token usage with conservative pre-authorization and refund rules.\n- Added configurable reasoning protocols, reasoning budgets, output limits, and reasoning visibility for text models. Billing now supports aggregate and mutually exclusive token buckets, including cache and reasoning prices.\n- Standardized storyboard output on `scenes[].shots[]`, introduced stable `shotKey` bidirectional mapping for video prompts, and added an optional direct-previous-shot continuity mode.\n- Standardized configurable submit and task-query paths across image, video, speech, and text providers, including proxy gateway prefixes and stricter path validation.\n- Migrated the Web application to Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Ant Design React, and Zustand while retaining the deployer-compatible `dist/public` static output.\n- Unified the visual and interaction patterns across model, provider, system configuration, error governance, release management, and system-management pages in the admin application.\n- Added source-build resource governance for Maven, Node.js, Go, and archive stages. CPU, memory, swap, process count, and I/O are constrained; builds slow down or pause under pressure and resume after recovery.\n- New installations now keep the admin access-code gate disabled by default. Administrators can enable it and configure the access path when needed.\n- Added a background-music type to official asset queries. Role, scene, and prop form APIs now return editable image prompts while remaining compatible with historical data shapes.\n- Local FFmpeg composition now preserves source-video audio and correctly mixes voice-over with looping background music. Resolution, subtitle sizing, media duration, rotation metadata, and timed-out child processes are handled consistently; video padding uses `tpad`, audio padding uses bounded `apad`, and multi-track mixing uses `amix normalize=0` with `alimiter`.\n- Docker, manual deployment, initialization SQL, and upgrade SQL now share the AID-managed FFmpeg 7.0.2 runtime at `/opt/aid-ffmpeg/current/ffmpeg` and `/opt/aid-ffmpeg/current/ffprobe`, so no post-install admin edit is required. Separate amd64 and arm64 artifacts are pinned by SHA-256 and validated for FFprobe, required encoders, filters, and a one-second audiovisual composition before activation. Failed installs preserve the previous runtime and valid installs are reused idempotently.\n- Docker and manual deployment now share automatic CJK font initialization. A verified system font is reused when available; otherwise AID installs the pinned Noto Sans SC 2.004 archive with SHA-256 verification and the original OFL license. The stable default path is `/opt/aid-fonts/current/aid-cjk-font`, and upgrades preserve non-empty custom font settings.\n- Fixed text-task pre-authorization and usage settlement, storyboard editor caret and reference insertion, video cover previews, project aspect-ratio propagation, terminal task recovery, scene-asset references, and other creation-flow reliability issues.\n- Added the repeatable `sql/v1.0.0-beta.6.sql` migration. Existing proxy paths, multipliers, and valid custom billing rules are preserved; historical duplicate configuration rows are consolidated before the configuration uniqueness constraint is restored.\n\n\u003e This is a Beta release. Upgrades build all three applications locally from the version tag. Back up the database and deployment configuration, then validate model billing, creation workflows, file storage, and online upgrades in a staging environment. Resource-constrained servers are throttled automatically, so builds may take longer.",
